        "original_id": "9bc06a75-b92a-583e-9ab3-6bcde9abe8ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Individualism of Gil Evans\n- People: Gil Evans, Miles Davis, Kurt Weill, Bob Dorough, John Lewis, Willie Dixon\n- Companies: Verve\n- Topics: big band arrangements, original compositions\n\nFacts:\n- Kurt Weill was born on March 2, 1900, and died on April 3, 1950.\n- Kurt Weill was a German composer who was active in Germany from the 1920s and later in the United States.\n- The Individualism of Gil Evans is an album by pianist, conductor, arranger, and composer Gil Evans.\n- The Individualism of Gil Evans was originally released on the Verve label in 1964.\n- The Individualism of Gil Evans features Gil Evans's big band arrangements of five original compositions, including two cowritten with Miles Davis.\n- The Individualism of Gil Evans also includes compositions by Kurt Weill, Bob Dorough, John Lewis, and Willie Dixon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
